{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '1,18p' global_memory_summary.md; sed -n '98,113p' paper.tex; sed -n '160,165p' paper.tex; sed -n '262,274p' paper.tex; tail -n 18 memory.md; ls global_memory; sed -n '1,95p' .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py\"","aggregated_output":"# Global Memory Summary\n\nUse as qualitative context only; do not use as quantitative grounding source.\n\n## Recent Entries\n\n- 2026-11-17 | step=idea | scope=idea\n  - summary: Selected Finite-N Nonlinear Control Variates with a Saturation Certificate; gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=Only a prospective hypothesis and algebraic design were produced, without an executed scientific finding warranting a distilled recommendation.\n  - evidence: Supplied and read incumbent manifest: correct=true, combined_score=0.4452117702819895. Histories and authoritative global JSONL were empty; conclusions had no prior findings. The named incumbent source file was unavailable. No task program, evaluator, benchmark, optimizer, package installation, or experiment was run. Alternatives considered were finite-dictionary simultaneous selection, pilot splitting, and stratified likelihood; cross-fitted score controls were chosen for label reuse and an explicit nonlinear-versus-affine headroom identity. Hard or affine scores may have no nonlinear gain; certified intervals may be wider. Both required JSON outputs were written with matching rubric arrays, and exactly one canonical local memory target was used.\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- 2026-11-17T17:58:08.354120+00:00 | step=evaluate | scope=attempt\n  - summary: harness evaluated program_1 exactly once\n  - evidence: combined_score=0.47579470916117633, correct=True; scientific acceptance passed; search metrics (data): {\"combined_score\": 0.47579470916117633, \"control_pass\": 1, \"correct\": true, \"empirical_coverage\": 0.9685714285714285, \"failure_fraction\": 0.0, \"mean_width_ratio\": 1.0426115450635955, \"minimum_case_coverage\": 0.94, \"nominal_coverage\": 0.95, \"scientific_validity\": 0, \"width_utility\": 0.4900804234468906}\n\\subsection{Held-out correction and shared-pool studentization}\nFor outer fold $\\mathcal I_k$, write $n_k=|\\mathcal I_k|$, $w_k=n_k/n$, and let $g_k$ be its fitted control. Define $r_i=Y_i-g_k(P_i)$ for $i\\in\\mathcal I_k$ and $H(u)=\\sum_k w_kg_k(u)$. The estimate and estimated variance are\n\\begin{align}\n \\widehat\\theta&=\\sum_k w_k\\overline r_k+\\overline H_U,\\label{eq:crossfit}\\\\\n \\widehat V&=\\sum_k\\frac{w_k^2}{n_k}s_k^2(r)\n                        +\\frac{s_U^2(H)}{N}.\\label{eq:studentizer}\n\\end{align}\nHere $s^2$ denotes sample variance with the usual degrees-of-freedom correction. The unlabeled term is the variance of a weighted \\emph{sum} of predictions evaluated on the same observations. Treating foldwise unlabeled means as independent would drop their covariance. Centering residuals within folds also avoids treating fold-specific prediction offsets as between-observation residual variation.\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/program.py#L215-L267]]\n\nFor the nonfallback return, the radius is $t_{1-\\alpha/2,\\,\\max(2,n-6)}\\sqrt{\\max(0,\\widehat V)}$. Binary endpoints are clipped to $[0,1]$. Constant scores in either pool trigger label-only inference. For binary outcomes, fewer than ten successes or fewer than ten failures also trigger that fallback: a Clopper--Pearson interval. The real-valued fallback uses a Student interval \\citep{Student}. Its exactness requires Gaussian outcomes, not merely real-valued measurements. These details matter when comparing widths: reference methods need not share the same critical value, variance convention, or fallback behavior.\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/program.py#L270-L305]]\n\nAn internal bounded-fold construction is also computed for binary inputs, but does \\emph{not} determine the returned interval. We therefore do not credit its concentration argument to the empirical intervals. Similarly, the presence of an exact binomial fallback does not make the full data-dependent fallback/Wald rule finite-sample exact. Figure~\\ref{fig:overview} separates these objects. Readable implementation evidence is included as \\path{source_evidence/program.py}, with the accompanying \\path{source_evidence/METHOD.md}; source locations and the reference implementation are indexed in the supplement.\n\n\\section{Variance Rationale and Validity Boundaries}\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/evaluate_final.py#L861-L895]]\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/resource_manifest.json#raw_shapes]]\n\nThe empirical condition uses the gene-expression example distributed with the fixed PPI reference release, whose source attribution is \\citet{Vaishnav}. Normalized duplicate outcome--score records are grouped before a deterministic development/final partition. Labeled and unlabeled observations are sampled independently with replacement from the final unique-record source. Consequently, its truth is the mean of that empirical source, not a claim about all promoter sequences or a new biological population. Underlying sequence strings are unavailable, so disjointness of normalized scalar records does not establish sequence-level disjointness.\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/resource_manifest.json#source]]\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/evaluate_final.py#L861-L873]]\n\\paragraph{What the comparison answers.}\nHolding all observation resources fixed leaves room to change how a score is used. The gene-expression result demonstrates a measured width reduction for the complete frozen procedure relative to the supplied references. The non-benefits show why that observation cannot be promoted to a generally better method. In particular, comparisons with an untuned correction can exaggerate the apparent value of learning a richer calibration. The tuned reference is indispensable for asking whether extra flexibility actually improves interval efficiency.\n\n\\paragraph{Validity remains a separate requirement.}\nThe original goal requires nominal coverage, not simply narrower intervals. The present evidence does not fully discharge that requirement. Deterministic-control variance identities are exact under their assumptions, while the learned-fold argument additionally requires stability and moments. The returned interval is asymptotic, its fallback is selected using the observed outcomes, and a separately computed bounded construction is not its certificate. The completed final qualification confirms the assessment's operational conditions, not these statistical assumptions. We therefore present a conditional efficiency study with an unresolved finite-sample validity boundary, rather than a generally valid interval-shortening solution.\n% @evidence[[paper_data.json#final_evaluation/outcome]]\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/METHOD.md#L144-L183]]\n\n\\paragraph{Identification and external validity.}\nThere is no controlled component ablation, so neither the role of the nonlinear basis nor the benefit of offset invariance is empirically isolated. The information controls alter the prediction information, not a single inference component. Only one real-valued empirical source is evaluated. Sampling normalized records with replacement gives a well-defined empirical-source estimand, but not a population-level biological validation or sequence-level independence guarantee. Heavy tails, distribution shift, informative labeling, predictor reuse of these labels, alternative sample sizes, and other scientific targets were not evaluated. The synthetic archives permit exact input replay, but the complete generating functions are not provided in the available manifest; we do not reconstruct them from condition names.\n\n\\paragraph{Uncertainty and reproducibility.}\nThe simultaneous binomial intervals are intentionally conservative. The paired bootstrap summarizes the completed repetitions, but its extreme percentile endpoints use a limited resampling budget; it should not be read as an exact simultaneous test. Multiple comparisons and estimator selection are different issues: adjusting result summaries does not validate the inner model-selection rule. Replacing Bonferroni allocation with a stepwise procedure such as \\citet{Holm} would change the reporting protocol and is not evaluated here. Finally, the upstream example archive has no separately declared data license in the supplied provenance. Reproduction from available local resources is documented, but redistribution rights require resolution before public release.\n- evidence: The preceding direct conclusions edit failed with OSError errno 30 on /workspace/investigation/conclusions.md before either the file or its history was modified. Thus the preceding final event overstated conclusions/history updates; neither occurred. The required local/global markdown and global JSONL memory appends did succeed. Existing conclusions remain unchanged; the strategy and this append-only log carry the new distinction between final measured conditional performance and untested component attribution. No attempt was made to bypass the read-only mount.\n- next_action: Proceed with paper_strategy.md and paper_strategy.json as validated framing outputs. If the shared conclusions artifact becomes writable later, qualify its source-only language using the independently audited final evidence. Stop reason: strategy_ready_validated; ancillary conclusions update unavailable.\n\n### 2026-11-17T20:16:29.505250+00:00 | step=paper | scope=paper\n- summary: Independent evidence audit confirms completed qualified evaluation; conditional-efficiency thesis retained.\n- evidence: final.qualification.outcome=qualified; 400 paired repeats over seven conditions; no downstream_study or ablation bundle. Scientific non-certification is explicitly conservative, not a diagnosed failure. Existing bibliography includes unscreened modern works and will be quarantined. Default apply_patch absent; a temporary compatible patch helper was provisioned outside the workspace.\n- next_action: Preserve inspectable sources, retrieve only exact permitted or historical references, draft within ICLR geometry. Conclusions gate=keep: no new recommendation beyond validated strategy.\n\n### 2026-11-17T20:32:11.870444+00:00 | step=draft | scope=paper\n- summary: Draft and 70 claim mappings written; scientific-evidence verifier reports zero dangling links.\n- evidence: All endpoint-derived means match stored summaries. Main paper preserves gene-expression gain, six non-benefits, rare-outcome zero widths and uncertain coverage. Twenty-five exact permitted/historical citations retained; ambiguous OpenAlex preprint matches were rejected and replaced with direct arXiv metadata. Official ICLR 2026 style retrieved. Concept placeholder is wired for deterministic orchestrator rendering only. Nine body pages compile by direct sanitized LaTeX; canonical compile wrapper rejects a symlink between two approved system TeX roots, and canonical figure validator lacks src.orchestrator. Neither issue is a manuscript grounding defect; independent checks will document these limitations instead of modifying validators.\n- next_action: Refine title and inspect layout, run independent schema/layout/input audits, complete reproduction bundle and final verification. Conclusions gate=keep: thesis unchanged.\n\n### 2026-11-17T20:39:51.818903+00:00 | step=final | scope=paper\n- summary: Writing-stage artifacts complete and consistent with grounded inputs; ready for orchestrator concept rendering.\n- evidence: paper.tex, paper.pdf (nine body pages, fourteen total), claims_grounding.json (70 mappings), figure_manifest.json, 25-reference bibliography/provenance, readable source_evidence and reproduction scripts are present. Canonical section/citation, claims and rendered-SI validators passed. Scientific-evidence verification has zero dangling references. Independent canonical-schema, density, standalone-language, bibliography, page-count and resolved TeX input audits passed. The unmodified canonical compile wrapper has a cross-approved-root system symlink false rejection; the canonical figure wrapper lacks src.orchestrator. These are disclosed in validation_report.json, not falsely reported as canonical passes. The required concept figure remains the explicitly orchestrator-owned placeholder and guarded prompt stub; no paid API was used. Final qualification is completed/qualified, but coverage remains uncertified; every non-benefit, rare-event caveat, missing ablation and source-identity limit is preserved. No scientific evaluation was rerun and paper_data.json was not edited.\n- next_action: Orchestrator should render fixed_resource_overview deterministically without paid enhancement, replace the placeholder, recompile and apply authoritative validation. Stop reason=writing_stage_complete. Conclusions gate=keep: no new scientific recommendation beyond the grounded strategy.\n\n_idea_generation\nattempts_history.jsonl\nbest_program_manifest.json\nconclusions.md\nconclusions_history.jsonl\nconclusions_other_workers.md\nevents.jsonl\nidea_generation_failures.jsonl\nideas\nideas_history.jsonl\nlatest_run_manifest.json\nmemory.jsonl\nmemory.md\nouter_state.json\ntask\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Append validated local/global memory entries for idea workflows.\n\nTwo modes:\n\n* default (event append) — appends one memory event to ``memory.md`` (local +\n  global) plus one JSONL record to ``memory.jsonl``. Existing behavior.\n* ``--write-conclusions`` — atomically replaces ``conclusions.md`` with a\n  validated single-paragraph distilled summary and appends a record to\n  ``conclusions_history.jsonl``. Validation rejects empty input,\n  multi-paragraph input, or input over 300 words.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport fcntl\nimport json\nimport os\nimport stat\nimport sys\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any\n\nCONCLUSIONS_WORD_LIMIT = 300\nGATE_TRIGGER_VALUES = (\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"d\")\n\nLOCAL_MEMORY_HEADERS = \"\"\"# Memory Log\n\n## Context\n## Idea Discoveries\n## Program Evaluations\n## Failures / Regressions\n## Next Hypotheses\n\"\"\"\n\nGLOBAL_MEMORY_HEADER = \"# Global Memory Log\\n\\n\"\n\n\ndef utc_now() -> str:\n    \"\"\"Return the current UTC timestamp string.\"\"\"\n    return datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()\n\n\ndef _load_event(*, event_json: str | None, event_file: Path | None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Load event.\"\"\"\n    if event_json:\n        parsed = json.loads(event_json)\n    elif event_file is not None:\n        parsed = json.loads(event_file.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    else:\n        raw = input().strip()\n        if not raw:\n            raise ValueError(\"missing event payload\")\n        parsed = json.loads(raw)\n    if not isinstance(parsed, dict):\n        raise ValueError(\"event payload must be a JSON object\")\n    return parsed\n\n\ndef _ensure_required_fields(event: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Ensure required fields.\"\"\"\n    normalized = dict(event)\n    if not isinstance(normalized.get(\"timestamp\"), str) or not normalized[\"timestamp\"].strip():\n        normalized[\"timestamp\"] = utc_now()\n\n    required_string_fields = (\"step\", \"scope\", \"summary\", \"evidence\", \"next_action\")\n    for key in required_string_fields:\n        value = normalized.get(key)\n        if not isinstance(value, str) or not value.strip():\n            raise ValueError(f\"missing required string field: {key}\")\n        normalized[key] = value.strip()\n\n    for key in (\"idea_id\", \"attempt_id\", \"program_id\"):\n        value = normalized.get(key)\n        if value is None:\n            continue\n        if not isinstance(value, str):\n            normalized[key] = str(value)\n        normalized[key] = normalized[key].strip() or None\n\n    metrics = normalized.get(\"metrics\")\n    if metrics is not None and not isinstance(metrics, dict):\n        raise ValueError(\"metrics must be an object when present\")\n    rubrics = normalized.get(\"rubrics\")\n    if rubrics is not None and not isinstance(rubrics, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"rubrics must be an array when present\")\n    tags = normalized.get(\"tags\")\n    if tags is not None:\n        if not isinstance(tags, list):\n            raise ValueError(\"tags must be an array when present\")\n        normalized[\"tags\"] = [str(item).strip() for item in tags if str(item).strip()]\n    return normalized\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
