{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sha256sum paper.tex references.bib references_provenance.json > /tmp/draft-gap-protected.sha256; cat global_memory/conclusions.md; rg -n 'local-memory|global-memory|add_argument' .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py | tail -n 20; sed -n '263,274p' paper.tex\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sha256sum paper.tex references.bib references_provenance.json > /tmp/draft-gap-protected.sha256; cat global_memory/conclusions.md; rg -n 'local-memory|global-memory|add_argument' .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py | tail -n 20; sed -n '263,274p' paper.tex\"","aggregated_output":"Audit cross-fit studentization for invariance to fold-specific additive shifts: controls that enter both the held-out correction and a weighted shared-unlabeled mean have offsets that cancel from the point estimate, whereas pooling held-out residuals across folds can retain arbitrary between-fold offsets in the variance. Weighted within-fold residual variances and a variance computed after averaging the shared-pool controls provide an offset-invariant candidate; justify learned-control covariance under explicit stability assumptions rather than claiming conditional independence or automatic coverage. Pair this audit with training-only comparisons against zero and affine controls before spending labels on nonlinear calibration, and isolate the mechanisms in ablations. As an untested alternative to hard family selection, compare smooth covariance stacking of unscaled affine and nonlinear controls using inner-held-out within-fold risk moments and a vanishing ridge; apply the finite-sample unlabeled-noise penalty only once, retain signed-control ranges, and freeze interval calibration in the comparison. Check near-tied and collinear controls explicitly, since smooth weighting does not itself establish nuisance stability or learned-control dominance. These are source-algebra diagnostics and prospective experiments, not evidence of measured narrowing or a coverage defect. Keep the overall rubric failure cause unknown when only aggregate metrics are available, and do not let an internal certificate stand in for validity of the returned interval.\n222:    parser.add_argument(\n228:    parser.add_argument(\"--event-json\", default=None, help=\"Event payload as JSON object string\")\n229:    parser.add_argument(\"--event-file\", default=None, help=\"Path to event JSON file\")\n230:    parser.add_argument(\n231:        \"--local-memory-md\",\n235:    parser.add_argument(\n236:        \"--global-memory-md\",\n240:    parser.add_argument(\n241:        \"--global-memory-jsonl\",\n246:    parser.add_argument(\n251:    parser.add_argument(\n256:    parser.add_argument(\n261:    parser.add_argument(\n267:    parser.add_argument(\n273:    parser.add_argument(\n278:    parser.add_argument(\n390:            \"append_memory: --global-memory-md and --global-memory-jsonl are required \"\nHolding all observation resources fixed leaves room to change how a score is used. The gene-expression result demonstrates a measured width reduction for the complete frozen procedure relative to the supplied references. The non-benefits show why that observation cannot be promoted to a generally better method. In particular, comparisons with an untuned correction can exaggerate the apparent value of learning a richer calibration. The tuned reference is indispensable for asking whether extra flexibility actually improves interval efficiency.\n\n\\paragraph{Validity remains a separate requirement.}\nThe original goal requires nominal coverage, not simply narrower intervals. The present evidence does not fully discharge that requirement. Deterministic-control variance identities are exact under their assumptions, while the learned-fold argument additionally requires stability and moments. The returned interval is asymptotic, its fallback is selected using the observed outcomes, and a separately computed bounded construction is not its certificate. The completed final qualification confirms the assessment's operational conditions, not these statistical assumptions. We therefore present a conditional efficiency study with an unresolved finite-sample validity boundary, rather than a generally valid interval-shortening solution.\n% @evidence[[paper_data.json#final_evaluation/outcome]]\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/METHOD.md#L144-L183]]\n\n\\paragraph{Identification and external validity.}\nThere is no controlled component ablation, so neither the role of the nonlinear basis nor the benefit of offset invariance is empirically isolated. The information controls alter the prediction information, not a single inference component. Only one real-valued empirical source is evaluated. Sampling normalized records with replacement gives a well-defined empirical-source estimand, but not a population-level biological validation or sequence-level independence guarantee. Heavy tails, distribution shift, informative labeling, predictor reuse of these labels, alternative sample sizes, and other scientific targets were not evaluated. The synthetic archives permit exact input replay, but the complete generating functions are not provided in the available manifest; we do not reconstruct them from condition names.\n\n\\paragraph{Uncertainty and reproducibility.}\nThe simultaneous binomial intervals are intentionally conservative. The paired bootstrap summarizes the completed repetitions, but its extreme percentile endpoints use a limited resampling budget; it should not be read as an exact simultaneous test. Multiple comparisons and estimator selection are different issues: adjusting result summaries does not validate the inner model-selection rule. Replacing Bonferroni allocation with a stepwise procedure such as \\citet{Holm} would change the reporting protocol and is not evaluated here. Finally, the upstream example archive has no separately declared data license in the supplied provenance. Reproduction from available local resources is documented, but redistribution rights require resolution before public release.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
